p.src:
For example, a covector transforms according to $V_m^{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}V_r^{(x)},$ and a mixed tensor according to $\bigl(T^m{}_{n}\bigr)_{(y)}
  =
  \frac{\partial y^m}{\partial x^r}
  \frac{\partial x^s}{\partial y^n}
  \bigl(T^r{}_{s}\bigr)_{(x)}.$ If every component on the right vanishes, every component on the left vanishes. Thus a tensor equation such as $T^m{}_{n}=0$ is either true in every coordinate system or false in every coordinate system. The same is true of an equality between tensors with matching indices.

