p.src:
A scalar field assigns one number to each point. Under a coordinate change the number is unchanged: $\phi^{(y)}(y)=\phi^{(x)}(x).$ The chain rule gives $\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial y^n}
  =
  \frac{\partial x^m}{\partial y^n}
  \frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x^m}.$ This is precisely the transformation law for a covector. The gradient of a scalar is therefore a tensor.

