p.src:
Let the $x$-coordinates be Cartesian for the moment and define $T_{mn}^{(x)}
  \stackrel{?}{=}
  \frac{\partial V_m^{(x)}}{\partial x^n}.$ If this were a genuine rank-two covariant tensor, its $y$-components would have to be $\begin{aligned}
  T_{mn}^{(y)}
  &=
  \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial x^s}{\partial y^n}
  T_{rs}^{(x)}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial x^s}{\partial y^n}
  \frac{\partial V_r^{(x)}}{\partial x^s}
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial V_r^{(x)}}{\partial y^n}.
  \end{aligned}$

