p.src:
Now calculate the ordinary derivative of the transformed covector directly. From Eq. , $\begin{aligned}
  \frac{\partial V_m^{(y)}}{\partial y^n}
  &=
  \frac{\partial}{\partial y^n}
  \left(
    \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}V_r^{(x)}
  \right)
  \nonumber\\
  &=
  \frac{\partial x^r}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial V_r^{(x)}}{\partial y^n}
  +
  \frac{\partial^2 x^r}
       {\partial y^n\partial y^m}
  V_r^{(x)}.
  \end{aligned}$ The first term is Eq. . The second term is new. It comes from differentiating the Jacobian that describes the moving coordinate basis.

