p.src:
Metric compatibility alone leaves the possibility of torsion. The connection used here is also taken to be torsion-free, $\Gamma^a{}_{bc}=\Gamma^a{}_{cb}.$ These two conditions determine the Levi–Civita connection uniquely. Permuting the indices in Eq. , adding two equations, subtracting the third, and raising one index gives $\boxed{
  \Gamma^a{}_{bc}
  =
  \frac{1}{2}g^{ad}
  \left(
    \partial_b g_{dc}
    +
    \partial_c g_{db}
    -
    \partial_d g_{bc}
  \right).}$

