p.src:
The transformation law contains an inhomogeneous second-derivative term: $\begin{aligned}
  \Gamma'^a{}_{bc}
  &=
  \frac{\partial y^a}{\partial x^r}
  \frac{\partial x^m}{\partial y^b}
  \frac{\partial x^n}{\partial y^c}
  \Gamma^r{}_{mn}
  \nonumber\\
  &\quad+
  \frac{\partial y^a}{\partial x^r}
  \frac{\partial^2 x^r}
       {\partial y^b\partial y^c}.
  \end{aligned}$ That inhomogeneous term is not a defect. It is exactly what cancels the corresponding term from differentiating tensor components.

