p.src:
Now differentiate the tangent vector itself. Set $V^n=t^n=\frac{dy^n}{ds}.$ Then $\frac{D t^n}{Ds}
  =
  \frac{d^2y^n}{ds^2}
  +
  \Gamma^n{}_{mr}
  \frac{dy^m}{ds}
  \frac{dy^r}{ds}.$ In flat Cartesian coordinates, this vanishes along a straight line because the tangent is constant. The tensorial form lets us use the same criterion in curvilinear coordinates and in genuinely curved spaces.

